{"_doc":"Per letter id (order P, I…VIII, E): words = 8 lemma keys for the \"today's words\" card, chosen from that letter by chapter band (P/I–II: A1–A2, III–V: B1, VI–VIII/E: B2–C1; widened by one band only when needed), never repeating a lemma of an earlier letter; no names, function words, single letters or words spelled exactly like their English gloss. spots = [{i: plate spot index, w: lemma key, was: old spot word}] — a replacement only for weak spot words (names, pronouns, verb forms, cognates, letters); the lemma occurs in the quoted message and names something in the picture; [] when none is needed or none fits. phrases = 1–2 expressions copied verbatim from the letter: {t: text, m: message index, ko, en, note_ko, note_en}.","lang":"es","letters":{"p1":{"words":["bueno","vida","sacar"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"campicos y buena vida","m":0,"ko":"작은 밭과 좋은 삶","en":"a few little fields and a good life","note_ko":"고야가 평생 되풀이한 꿈. -ico 는 아라곤 말투의 ‘작은’ 꼴이에요.","note_en":"Goya's lifelong dream; -ico is the Aragonese ‘little’ ending."}]},"p2":{"words":["vez","escuela"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"tal vez","m":0,"ko":"아마","en":"perhaps","note_ko":"‘아마, 어쩌면’. 문장 앞에 와요.","note_en":"‘Perhaps, maybe’; usually at the start."}]},"p3":{"words":["parecer"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"parece que","m":0,"ko":"~인 것 같다","en":"it seems that","note_ko":"parecer + que: 보이는 대로 짐작할 때.","note_en":"parecer + que: to say how things look."}]},"p4":{"words":["mujer"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Mi mujer","m":0,"ko":"내 아내","en":"my wife","note_ko":"mi 는 ‘나의’. 고야는 편지에서 아내를 늘 이렇게 불러요.","note_en":"mi = my; Goya always calls her this in his letters."}]},"c1-l1":{"words":["decir","mejor","pensar","dar","gracia","tener","tiempo","hacer"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Me alegro","m":0,"ko":"기뻐","en":"I'm glad","note_ko":"alegrarse: ‘기뻐하다’. Me alegro que … 로 기쁜 까닭을 말해요.","note_en":"alegrarse: to be glad; Me alegro (de) que … gives the reason."},{"t":"te doy gracias","m":1,"ko":"고마워","en":"I thank you","note_ko":"dar gracias: ‘고맙다고 하다’. 그냥 Gracias 라고도 해요.","note_en":"dar gracias: to give thanks; plain Gracias also works."}]},"c1-l2":{"words":["amistad","merecer","cansar","esperanza","amigo","escapar"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Infinitas gracias","m":0,"ko":"끝없이 고마워","en":"endless thanks","note_ko":"아주 큰 고마움. 오늘은 Muchas gracias 를 더 많이 써요.","note_en":"Very warm thanks; today Muchas gracias is more common."},{"t":"ya estoy bueno","m":2,"ko":"이제 다 나았어","en":"I'm well again now","note_ko":"estar bueno: ‘(몸이) 괜찮다’. ya 는 ‘이제’.","note_en":"estar bueno: to be well (in health); ya = now, already."}]},"c1-l3":{"words":["orden","señor","mano","tocar","gente","oír","fin","saber"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"De orden del señor","m":0,"ko":"~ 님의 지시에 따라","en":"by order of Señor","note_ko":"공식 글의 첫머리 말투예요.","note_en":"A formal opening for an official note."},{"t":"su servidor","m":1,"ko":"삼가 드림","en":"your servant","note_ko":"옛 편지의 맺음말. 오늘날 Atentamente 와 비슷해요.","note_en":"An old letter closing, like today's Atentamente."}]},"c1-l4":{"words":["juego","rey","ir","salir","baile","querer","poner"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Querido Martín","m":0,"ko":"사랑하는 마르틴","en":"Dear Martín","note_ko":"편지 첫머리. 여자에게는 Querida.","note_en":"A letter opening; to a woman, Querida."},{"t":"En fin","m":1,"ko":"아무튼","en":"anyway","note_ko":"말을 정리하고 넘어갈 때.","note_en":"To wrap up and move on."}]},"c1-l5":{"words":["pena","valer","contar","gustar","gusto","ver","mayor"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"por no tener tiempo","m":0,"ko":"시간이 없어서","en":"because I had no time","note_ko":"por + 동사원형: ‘~해서’ 까닭.","note_en":"por + infinitive gives the reason."},{"t":"gracia de Dios","m":2,"ko":"하느님 은혜","en":"the grace of God","note_ko":"por la gracia de Dios: 고마운 일을 말할 때.","note_en":"por la gracia de Dios: for a blessing."}]},"c1-l6":{"words":["casa","necesitar","mueble","mesa","silla","sartén"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"no necesito","m":0,"ko":"필요 없어","en":"I don't need","note_ko":"no + 동사: 부정. necesitar de 는 옛 말투예요.","note_en":"no + verb makes it negative; necesitar de is old usage."},{"t":"todo lo demás","m":1,"ko":"나머지는 다","en":"everything else","note_ko":"lo demás: ‘나머지’.","note_en":"lo demás: the rest."}]},"c1-l7":{"words":["estimar","encargar","sepultura","triste","repetir","conocer","caso"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"te lo estima infinito","m":0,"ko":"네게 무척 고마워해","en":"is ever so grateful to you","note_ko":"estimar: ‘소중히 여기다, 고마워하다’.","note_en":"estimar: to value, to be grateful for."},{"t":"lo hagas","m":1,"ko":"그렇게 해 줘","en":"you do it","note_ko":"hacer 의 접속법. 부탁 · 바람에 써요.","note_en":"Subjunctive of hacer, for requests and wishes."}]},"c2-l1":{"words":["trabajo","mirar","solo","deber","encontrar","dejar","razón","cosa"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"con su mayor respeto","m":0,"ko":"깊은 존경을 담아","en":"with his greatest respect","note_ko":"청원서의 정중한 첫머리 말.","note_en":"A formal opening for a petition."},{"t":"el honor de un profesor es cosa muy delicada","m":3,"ko":"화가의 명예는 아주 섬세한 것","en":"the honour of a professional is a very delicate thing","note_ko":"ser cosa + 형용사: ‘~한 것이다’.","note_en":"ser cosa + adjective: ‘is a … thing’."}]},"c2-l2":{"words":["carta","pasado","nuevo","acuerdo","pasar","dicho","justo","año"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Muy señor mío","m":0,"ko":"삼가 아룁니다","en":"Dear Sir","note_ko":"공식 편지의 첫머리. 오늘날 Estimado señor.","note_en":"A formal letter opening; today Estimado señor."},{"t":"muchos años","m":2,"ko":"오래","en":"many years","note_ko":"Dios guarde a … muchos años: 옛 편지의 맺음 축원.","note_en":"An old closing blessing: ‘God keep you many years’."}]},"c2-l3":{"words":["llegar","iglesia","grande","corte","llevar","fuego","motivo","feliz"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"llegó el tiempo","m":0,"ko":"때가 왔어","en":"the time has come","note_ko":"llegar 의 단순 과거 (llegó).","note_en":"Simple past of llegar."},{"t":"en fin","m":2,"ko":"한마디로","en":"in short","note_ko":"말을 정리할 때.","note_en":"To sum up."}]},"c2-l4":{"words":["noticia","hermana","juicio","capaz","padre","escribir","médico","modo"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Martín mío","m":0,"ko":"내 마르틴","en":"my dear Martín","note_ko":"이름 + mío: 다정하게 부르는 말.","note_en":"Name + mío: an affectionate address."},{"t":"el mejor día","m":2,"ko":"언제라도","en":"any day now","note_ko":"여기서는 ‘곧, 어느 날 갑자기’.","note_en":"Here: ‘any day now’."}]},"c2-l5":{"words":["conde","tarde","señoría","hora","después","comer","venir"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"no diga nada","m":0,"ko":"아무 말도 말라","en":"not to say anything","note_ko":"no + 접속법: 부정 명령 · 부탁.","note_en":"no + subjunctive: a negative request."},{"t":"le debo tanto","m":1,"ko":"신세를 많이 졌어","en":"I owe him so much","note_ko":"deber: ‘빚지다’.","note_en":"deber: to owe."}]},"c2-l6":{"words":["señora","niño","niña","último","mes","oro","sentir","volver"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Acabo de llegar","m":0,"ko":"막 돌아왔어","en":"I've just arrived","note_ko":"acabar de + 동사원형: ‘막 ~했다’.","note_en":"acabar de + infinitive: to have just done."},{"t":"son unos ángeles","m":3,"ko":"다들 천사 같아","en":"they're angels","note_ko":"unos + 명사: ‘정말 ~같은 사람들’.","note_en":"unos + noun: ‘real …’."}]},"c2-l7":{"words":["acabar","mandar","celebrar","cuadro","hablar","esperado","profesor","arte"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"los últimos retoques","m":1,"ko":"마지막 손질","en":"the last touches","note_ko":"retoque: 그림을 다듬는 손질.","note_en":"retoque: a finishing touch."},{"t":"hacen lo mismo","m":2,"ko":"다 그래","en":"are doing the same","note_ko":"lo mismo: ‘같은 것’.","note_en":"lo mismo: the same thing."}]},"c3-l1":{"words":["descubrir","empezar","justicia","asegurar","voz","correr","asunto","bastante"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"se empieza a hablar","m":0,"ko":"사람들 입에 오르내리기 시작했어","en":"people are starting to talk","note_ko":"se + 동사: ‘사람들이 ~한다’.","note_en":"Impersonal se: ‘people …’."},{"t":"me acuerdo mucho de","m":1,"ko":"자꾸 생각나","en":"I keep remembering","note_ko":"acordarse de: ‘~을 기억하다’.","note_en":"acordarse de: to remember."}]},"c3-l2":{"words":["luz","guapo","ayer","término","lograr","día"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"dio a luz","m":0,"ko":"낳았어","en":"gave birth","note_ko":"dar a luz: ‘아이를 낳다’.","note_en":"dar a luz: to give birth."},{"t":"Dios quiera","m":1,"ko":"부디","en":"God grant","note_ko":"Dios quiera (que) + 접속법: 간절한 바람.","note_en":"Dios quiera (que) + subjunctive: a heartfelt wish."}]},"c3-l3":{"words":["fortuna","concepto","inteligente","público","participar","menor","cierto"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Es cierto que","m":0,"ko":"~인 건 사실이야","en":"it's true that","note_ko":"확실한 일을 말할 때.","note_en":"To state something as true."},{"t":"hasta ahora","m":1,"ko":"아직","en":"so far","note_ko":"‘지금까지’.","note_en":"‘Until now’."}]},"c3-l4":{"words":["desear","ordenar","causar","palacio","suceder","precisamente","arriba","creer"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"no he podido desear más","m":0,"ko":"더 바랄 게 없었어","en":"I couldn't have wished for more","note_ko":"현재완료 + 부정.","note_en":"Present perfect with no."},{"t":"con más sosiego","m":2,"ko":"좀 더 차분히","en":"with more calm","note_ko":"con + 명사: 방법.","note_en":"con + noun: how something is done."}]},"c3-l5":{"words":["izquierda","princesa","seguir","diversión","despedida","tren","vista","detrás"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"muy contento","m":0,"ko":"아주 흐뭇하게","en":"very happy","note_ko":"contento: ‘기쁜, 만족한’.","note_en":"contento: glad, pleased."},{"t":"me acordé de ti","m":1,"ko":"네 생각이 났어","en":"I thought of you","note_ko":"acordarse de 의 단순 과거.","note_en":"Simple past of acordarse de."}]},"c3-l6":{"words":["julio","estudio","servir","ganar","sueldo","auxilio","posible","atención"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"con la debida veneración","m":0,"ko":"마땅한 공경을 담아","en":"with due veneration","note_ko":"청원서의 정중한 말투.","note_en":"Formal language of a petition."},{"t":"ganar el sustento","m":3,"ko":"생계를 꾸리다","en":"to earn a living","note_ko":"ganar: ‘벌다’.","note_en":"ganar: to earn."}]},"c3-l7":{"words":["secreto","domingo","bajar","contrario","ejemplo","uso","primero","lugar"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"en primer lugar","m":0,"ko":"1순위로","en":"in first place","note_ko":"순서를 말할 때.","note_en":"To say the order."},{"t":"poco provecho y mucho honor","m":1,"ko":"돈은 적고 명예는 크지","en":"little profit and much honour","note_ko":"poco · mucho 의 맞세움.","note_en":"The contrast poco / mucho."}]},"c4-l1":{"words":["enviar","buscar","ocurrir","subir","coger","causa","hermano","jefe"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"ya soy Pintor del Rey","m":0,"ko":"드디어 왕의 화가가 됐어","en":"I'm Painter to the King now","note_ko":"ya + 현재: ‘이제 ~이다’.","note_en":"ya + present: ‘now I am’."},{"t":"He dado gracias","m":3,"ko":"감사를 드렸어","en":"I've thanked","note_ko":"dar gracias 의 현재완료.","note_en":"Present perfect of dar gracias."}]},"c4-l2":{"words":["anterior","largo","aprender","imaginar","parar","caballo","medio","camino"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Querido Martín","m":0,"ko":"사랑하는 마르틴","en":"Dear Martín","note_ko":"편지의 첫머리.","note_en":"A letter opening."},{"t":"aunque era ancho","m":2,"ko":"넓긴 해도","en":"wide as it was","note_ko":"aunque + 과거: ‘~이긴 했지만’.","note_en":"aunque + past: ‘although it was’."}]},"c4-l3":{"words":["alma","viaje","disponer","cumplir","encargo","tamaño","tomar","edad"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"tomo la pluma","m":0,"ko":"펜을 들어","en":"I take up my pen","note_ko":"편지를 쓰기 시작할 때의 말.","note_en":"A phrase for starting to write."},{"t":"sin duda alguna","m":2,"ko":"꼭","en":"without any doubt","note_ko":"강한 약속.","note_en":"A firm promise."}]},"c4-l4":{"words":["rueda","matar","andar","calle","comprar","par","casi"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Ya no quiero","m":0,"ko":"이제 … 싫어","en":"I don't want … any more","note_ko":"ya no + 동사: ‘이제는 ~ 않다’.","note_en":"ya no + verb: no longer."},{"t":"un par de mulas","m":1,"ko":"노새 두 마리","en":"a pair of mules","note_ko":"un par de: ‘두어, 한 쌍의’.","note_en":"un par de: a pair of, a couple of."}]},"c4-l5":{"words":["alegrar","pensamiento","oferta","mantener","ofrecer","voluntad","claro","mundo"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"hablemos claros","m":0,"ko":"솔직히 말하자","en":"let